{}	base	set06a-DEM00	Yes	Most social traditions have been introduced from Sicily: food; dress; religious functions and "outside festivities", like processions, street decorations, fireworks, the crib; traditional children's games, the Imnarja (luminaria) on the feast of Saints Peter and Paul (an agricultural show and folklore night).\nRegarding gifts, Sicilians would normally present typical sweets or Caltagirone pottery to Maltese persons during visits or as a show of gratitude for some favour. The Maltese would present some local handcraft, like glass works or spirits (like whisky).	\N	6	6	2	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
