{}	base	set32-DEM29_DEME29-1	No	Monogamy is the customary marriage pattern in both Yurok and Karuk speaking communities. When a man died his widow remained in his family, often marrying a brother of her deceased husband for a reduced bride price. These customs led to sequential marriages, not simultaneous marriages. Extramarital relationships were not considered acceptable, and a fine was traditionally owed to the husband for a wife's infidelity.	\N	1014	1014	179	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
