{}	base	set01-DEM96	In regards to the multiple origins and non-Salish aspects of Nuxalk, note that: (a) the Salish portion of this language appears to have originated in the vicinity of the Olympic peninsula (southern maritime British Columbia – northwest Washington State west of the Cascades); (b) Nuxalk has a number of Tsimshianic and other “Penutian” (including Chinook Proper) features and morphemes not shared with other Salish; (c) there was once regular contact – resulting in vocabulary copying – with Athabascan populations east, northeast, and north of the Nuxalk domain.	\N	\N	1617	1617	\N	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
