{}	base	set24-DEM96	Pilagá, Mocoví, Wichí. "the communication phenomena among the traditional peoples of the Gran Chaco undoubtedly depend upon the referred social model characterized by progressively inclusive unities, of which more or less stable alliances of bands -which traditionally wandered around a specific territory- were the most extense political groupings. Besides, because inside them most exchanges of any kind happend, they defined the ares of solidarity and common historical awareness [...] These band alliances, which we regularly call 'tribes', DEMEographically restricted to around a few thousand individuals, concentrated most circuits of marriage, good and linguistic exchanges. On the other hand, there was communication of an intensity that was quantitatively less and qualitatively different among neighbouring tribes, be it circumstantial alliances with extra-tribal purposes, or reciprocal theft of goods or woman and children." (Braunstein 2005)\nIt is estimated that since pre-colonial times, before contact with the Spanish Group.	\N	\N	1632	1632	\N	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
