{}	base	set16-DFK39	[q2o2answer] women often relocate to [q2o1answer] locations	Like the Chipaya, the Aymara are also patri- or virilocal, meaning that an Aymara woman married to a Chipaya usually moves to his place. However, given that until quite recently, the Chipaya were (and possibly still are) despised by their Aymara neighbours, it may also be possible that the couple moves either to the woman's place (i.e. an Aymara location) or to a new place altogether (e.g. La Paz or another place with equal economic chances) but this is more of an educated guess.	\N	2831	2800	484	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
