{}	base	set23-DFK99	Intermarriages between Sibe and Uighur people are rather rare due to the fact that the Uighurs are Moslems, while the Sibe are traditionally Buddhist ans shamanists. There is a general notion among the Sibe people that the customs of both groups differ to the extent of making cohabitation difficult. However, Uighur women are considered beautiful by Sibe men and a certain number of intermarriages has been occuring all the time. Due to the scarcity of such cases it is difficult to make generalizations in this respect. I have personally known only two Sibe men with Uighur wives, and heard about some five more. Intermarriages with non-Sibe have been more frequent in enclaves of Sibe outside the main area of their habitation. However, the first thing our consultants always mentioned when asked about intermarriages with Uighur was that Sibe would rather mainly marry Mongols and Kazakhs (in addition to Chinese)  than Uighurs.\nIntermarriages have been happening since 1800 to the present – they still happen today.	\N	\N	3000	2931	\N	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
