{}	base	set03-DKN00	No	K. and W. rarely if at all share the same space of knowledge transfer (in our case schools). Administrative zonal boundaries are drawn along ethnic boundaries in Ethiopia. Schools are organised by the zones. In primary level schools, the medium of instruction is the local language (K. and W. in our case), on the secondary level, the medium of instruction is English. There might only be children living at the linguistic/ethnic boundaries between K. and W. that attend the same school (but this is very likely to be exceptional). In the religious context, no spaces are shared either. If K. and W. attend the same space of knowledge transfer (which is definitely exceptional), then the instruction is done in Amharic.	\N	3032	2963	514	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
