{}	base	set06b-DLC27	Influence is somewhat exerted	I'm inferring, and additionally there may have been considerable variation between the urban and rural areas. I'd see the rural areas as 'belonging' to the Maltese, at least more than the urban areas (see my comment above). Especially during the Order's rule, the Knights were definitely in charge, e.g. trying to segregate living areas according to social status and at times prohibiting Maltese from moving into already overcrowded cities (cf. Blouet 1967: 102, 108, 115). However, I chose the response 'influence is somewhat exerted', since I believe that the Knights couldn't regulate all everyday activities.	\N	6251	6094	1039	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
