{}	base	set32-DLC32	Some people	Due to the geography of the Yurok area, opportunities for contact are most frequent near the confluence of the Klamath and Trinity Rivers, with fewer opportunities for contact lower on the Klamath River and still fewer along the coast. This is reflected in the marriage patterns reported by Waterman and Kroeber (1934). Karuk individuals marry into upriver Yurok communities most frequently, mid-river Yurok communities less frequently, and are very rarely married into Yurok communities near the mouth of the Klamath River or along the Pacific Coast. As a result of this geographic pattern, opportunities for contact are distributed unevenly over this space and not all Yurok people would have historically had many opportunities for contact with Karuk speakers.	\N	6394	6237	1059	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
