{}	base	set20-DTR02_DTR02-1	Yes	While the Santali people used to sell raw materials like woods, kendu leaves for making indigenous cigar and sal leaves for making leaf-cups and leaf-plates used in the sweet shops and road side eateries along with primary produce like forest vegetables (this continues even today) the Bengali people sell primary produce like rice, flour, oil, salt, sugar etc. and manufactured items like dress materials and earthen jars and kitchen utensils. Agricultural instruments are also sold by the Bengali sellers. Now-a- days the Bengali sellers also sell aluminum utensils to the Santali people.	\N	6670	6462	1086	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
