{}	base	set33-DTR03_DTR03-1	Yes	Aleuts lived in family groups, but did not apparently have the moiety system of Pacific Northwest groups. It was not unheard of for young men to travel far to obtain rare trade items for their sweethearts at home, but there is no evidence of restrictions on who could trade among the males, although wealthy males had more opportunities to trade.  Also, orphans and dependents were not in a position to trade. Women could be traded, as could slaves.	\N	6873	6665	1104	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
