{}	base	set06b-DTR06	At places which belong to some other group	My argument for choosing 'At places belong to some other group' is the same as in DLB (see my comment to DLB05). Recap: Trade was most frequent in urban harbour areas (see my comments to DTR03 and DTR32) and although these places are located in Malta, I'm inferring they were more associated foreign groups (Sicilians and others) in general. Their construction (especially fortification) was mostly a venture of the foreign powers (Norman, Genoese, Aragonese, Angevin, Order of St John..., on building cities cf. Brincat: 2021: 76, 156, 217) and these cities were the main hubs where Maltese people had contact with foreigners.	\N	7136	6928	1132	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
