{}	base	set08-DTR06	This is highly contextual	Up until the 1970s or so, individual men with trading partners in the other language group traded at either their own or their partner’s village. Since the 1970s this type of trade has declined in importance. Trading today is still actively done by women in groups at traditional market sites scattered around the edges of the Washkuk Hills. Trade also takes place at modern markets at Ambunti township, where goods are sold for cash, rather than exchanged for goods of equivalent value.	\N	7138	6930	1133	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
