{}	base	set20-DTR0a	For the last 60-70 years or even before.	Before dispersal in different places the Santali people were hunter-gatherers and through the means of forest produce, they used to earn their living. When they were not distributed in contiguous areas of the neighboring communities like Bengali, they used to travel miles away from the place of their concentration to sell forest produce and woods in the weekly markets. In earlier days when the money economy did not infiltrate in their society, they used to depend on barter system. In the process they used to collect salt and occasionally oil in exchange of woods and forest produce.	\N	7245	7037	\N	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
