{}	base	set08-DTR14	Often	Today, as formerly, women trade regularly throughout the year but more commonly during the wet season (roughly Nov to May). During the wet season the flooding of lagoons makes the traditional Kwoma woman’s method of fishing impossible. This involves wading with hand-nets. Today Kwoma men and women are increasingly using canoes to fish with gill-nets during the wet season but this seems to have had little impact overall on the frequency of women’s trade. More detailed research on this topic needs to be undertaken.	\N	7393	7185	1167	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
