{}	base	set06a-DTR17	Influence is exerted very little	Malta was governed from Sicily between 1127 and 1530, therefore Sicilian political, social and economic influence was strong. It became an autonomous state in 1530 when emperor Charles V granted it as a fief to the Knights of St John and therefore Sicilian political influence stopped and is never exerted nowadays.	\N	7454	7246	1181	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
{}	base	set06b-DTR17	Influence is somewhat exerted	I've chosen a middle-ground option here. I'm suspecting that the Maltese did not exert much influence, if they traded mostly agricultural products and Sicilians traded more valuable goods (see my comment to DTR02). Also, Malta depended on Sicilian wheat.	\N	7455	7247	1180	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
