{}	base	set16-DTR17	Influence is somewhat exerted	This is difficult to answer and I am unsure about the amount influence that can be exerted by the Chipaya people. Thus, the following is more of an educated guess than a hard and fast fact. Prices of the goods traded at the local markets in, say, Oruro and La Paz are commonly known by the local population (that includes the Chipaya people), so if an outrageous price was set for an item the Chipaya people know to be purchasable at a more moderate price, they would simply walk away and buy it somewhere else. Thus, I guess the Chipaya people can exert as much influence as any 'campesino', i.e. an inhabitant of the rural, poor and underdeveloped Bolivian highland.	\N	7465	7257	1180	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
