{}	base	set29-OH1	Yes	Seasonal contact with Macassan fishermen occurred during this time period. This is commonly discussed and had wide-ranging impacts, including on local mobility. Coastal groups came together to trade and work with the Macassans on harvesting trepang.\n\nNo natural disasters I know of in the selected time period – although it is of interest that coastal inundation seems to have occurred over 7000 years ago and is still noted in stories around the island in oral narratives. Underwater sacred sites known about by local groups may have originally been on land but information handed down for a remarkably long time.\n\nObviously the most calamitous and impactful social upheaval is that of European invasion in the late 18th century, but that is after the focus time period.	\N	8737	8487	1371	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
