{}	base	set29-OI1_OI1-3	Yes	Clan groups are affiliated with (usually) one language, and sometimes higher level groupings of clans (sometimes called clan aggregates or companies) may also be associated with a single language, but they may well be associated with more than one (e.g. Maringa --> Burarra and Yan-nhangu). \n\nThe Burarra language as an expression of identity is most stable at the clan level, but post-colonially higher level groupings have become more important. Now, groups of clans are labelled with Burarra 'dialect' labels (e.g. An-barra, Martay) and Burarra as an identity subsuming all Burarra-speaking clans has become somewhat more salient.	\N	8842	8592	1380	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
