{}	base	set06b-OI6	Neither positive nor negative	Hard to assess. A great number of loanwords came from Sicilian, both in high and low registers (administration, law, taxation, religion, but also construction, handcrafts, manufactured goods). In addition to loanwords, Sicilian influenced the vowel system of Maltese, and to a lesser extent morphosyntactic features (overview in Brincat 2021: 103–143). There was no clear language policy to promote the use of Sicilian (or to substitute the use of Maltese with Sicilian), but the linguistic transfer spread through "persistent process which was a peaceful one because if followed material and social progress" (Brincat 2021: 116) – I'm interpreting from this that the attitudes were at least "open", even if "positive" might not be exactly the right term.	\N	8958	8708	1393	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
