{}	base	set12-OL3	Yes, in a standardised way	see also 26.9 [QID: OI3] The majority of zazakî-script follows standard zazakî. That means if written, then mostly in the standard (based on the Vate group). However, this is limited to the part of the population that has enjoyed some kind of education on Zazakî. The majority of Zazas are illiterate in their mother tongue. That part of course communicates in a non-standard way (e.g. in a chat messenger).	\N	9376	9126	1443	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
