{}	base	set17-OL3	Yes, in a non-standardised way	Otomi has a writing standard, which was created by bilingual teachers of the different dialect varieties of Otomi in collaboration with INALI in 2014. However, very few Otomi speakers know and use it.	\N	9381	9131	1442	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
