{}	base	set11-OS6	Agricultural, permanent	The basis of subsistence which determines the rhythm of all other activities is definitely rice, with permanent fields, whose importance is crucial. I remember someone saying that without rice fields, there are no Bainounk. The work on the fields is traditionally organised by generation- and gender-based work groups. Women plant and harvest, while men do the heavy earthshifting and digging.\n Other crops, such as manioc, peanuts, citrus fruits are also cultivated but less intensely and some with shifting field patterns by clearing forest and letting it overgrow in cycles in order to preserve the soil. Fishing and hunting is practiced by skilled individuals, most households have pigs, goats and chickens for domestic purposes. Some wild plants and animals are gathered in the forest or the mangrove such as crabs, wild fruits, some sort of yam.	\N	9550	9300	1471	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
