{}	base	set18-OS9	Infrequently	I have based my answer on this sentence in Rationale OS9: "In dense social networks people interact mostly with other in-group people, that is, with their intimates". Living in small bands is effectively a society of intimates. People would have met new people only in large ceremonial gatherings, which would have taken place infrequently. However due to the fact that there are a large number of social groups that people participate in, each band would have always included people who identified each other as members of a different group in some way, and as the same group in other ways.	\N	9627	9377	1485	\N	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
