9558	{"comment": "Between one and two centuries in the religious domain for Focus muslims (with Macro-Neighbour being the main vehicle of Islam).\\u2028\\nOne century approximately for formal education, which appeared in the Focus area in the 1920s with the establishment of the first (christian) mission schools, that resorted mainly to Macro-Neighbour as the medium of instruction.", "start": 1800, "end": 2020}	base	DKN0aNset10	\N	\N	19	367	11	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
9559	{"comment": "Actually difficult to say, but probably since the immigration of the Turkic-speaking tribes in Anatolia. There is a theory, that that the appearance of Zazas in the areas where they live today seems to have been connected with waves of migration of Zazas from the highlands of G\\u012bl\\u0101n province in Iran (Deylam) during the 10th-12th centuries, as mentioned by Asatrian (1995). However, there is no extra-linguistic data on a possible migration of the Zazak\\u00ee speakers. Whether and when they migrated from where or not is very hypothetical, which a) is based on morphosyntactic correlations between Zazak\\u00ee and some languages of the Caspian Sea and b) erroneously goes back to the fact that the tribal names Dimil\\u00ee and Daylam are the same (a basically refuted fallacy, which dates from the beginning of the 20th century). If the Zaza or language originated in the Daylam region, the split is likely at least a millennium ago, if not older.", "start": 1000, "end": 2020}	base	DKN0aNset12	\N	\N	23	367	13	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
