9563	{"comment": "The Alorese and the Adang are in contact since the Alorese settled on the coast of the Alor peninsula (also known as Alor Bird\\u2019s Head), the Adang inhabited that area previous to the arrival of the Alorese.. Wellfelt (2016:273) reports that, in 1971, the lineage of the Alorese royal house in the village of Alor Besar counted seventeen generations. If we allow for generations of 25 years (17 x 25 = 425 years), the establishment of the Alorese village Alor Besar must have taken place about 425 years before 1971, roughly in 1550.", "start": 1550, "end": 2020}	base	DKN0aNset19	\N	\N	37	367	20	\N	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	2026-09-27 10:36:49.766157+02	t
